# Progress Log

## 2026-08-28 — Guestbook authorization handoff

- Added `handoff.md` with the owner-only Apps Script authorization steps required to activate the deployed guestbook.
- Updated `.config/ai/handoff.ai` with the same current task and completion criteria.

## 2026-08-28 — Visitor guestbook implementation and deployment

- Added routed **Sign the guestbook** and **See the guestbook** pages backed by server-side Apps Script functions.
- Added a shared tested validation module: names and cities are normalized, required, limited to 80 characters, and rendered with DOM text nodes to prevent HTML injection.
- Added private Google Sheet integration via the untracked `GUESTBOOK_SPREADSHEET_ID` Script Property, the `Visitors` worksheet, append locking, and a short duplicate-submission throttle. The underlying Sheet is not embedded or exposed to visitors.
- Added build and validation tests. Validation: `npm run build`, `npm test` (25 passing), and `git diff --check`.
- Pushed the source and redeployed the existing public Apps Script deployment at versions 2 and 3. The initial Sheets setup awaits one owner authorization in the Apps Script editor; anonymous `?page=view` returns Google access denied until that approval is completed.

## 2026-08-27 — Visitor guestbook specification

- Created SpecKit feature `0.007-visitor-guestbook` on branch `feature/visitor-guestbook`.
- Defined a public name-and-city submission page, a read-only public guestbook view backed by a private owner-controlled Google Sheet, validation, privacy, and approval boundaries.
- No application code, spreadsheet, or deployment was changed in this planning step.

## 2026-08-27 — Startup permission gates

- Added SpecKit entry `0.006-startup-permission-gates`.
- `start.ai` now requires explicit human permission before tool installation or upgrades, authentication, Apps Script project creation, deployment, or other material external changes. It still permits read-only diagnostics and safe checkout-local remediation without a separate confirmation.
- Added an automated assertion for the permission policy.
- Validation: `npm test` (22 passing) and `git diff --check`.

## 2026-08-27 — Fresh-clone public Hello World onboarding completed

- Installed the latest Node.js and npm, restored project dependencies, and installed SpecKit (`specify 1.0.2.dev0`).
- Enabled the Apps Script API for the authenticated project owner, authenticated clasp with credentials stored only in ignored `.secrets/.clasprc.json`, and created a new standalone Apps Script project.
- Published the first deployment locally as permitted for a new nohost project. The deployment ID remains untracked in the ignored `.clasp.json`.
- Validation: `npm run doctor` passed with `Develop: ready`, `Deploy: ready`, and `Public Hello World: visible` (HTTP 200).

## 2026-08-27 — Fresh-install Hello World onboarding

- README now leads with an AI prompt and success check (`Public Hello World: visible`).
- `start.ai` requires finishing first-run on a fresh clone (nvm, Apps Script API, clasp login, **standalone** create, `npm run deploy`) before other feature work.
- Doctor remediations no longer use invalid `--type webapp`. First-time local deploy of a new nohost script is allowed; GitHub production stays separate.
- Validation: `npm test`.

## 2026-08-27 — Track latest Node and npm

- Replaced the pinned Node 20 engine with `.nvmrc` containing `node` (nvm's latest alias) and GitHub Actions `node-version: latest`.
- `npm run doctor` now includes `npm doctor versions`, so the gate follows npm's current latest Node/npm instead of a major number.
- Validation: `npm test` after the change.

## 2026-08-27 — CI latest-npm gate

- GitHub Actions `setup-node` with `node-version: latest` installed Node 26.8.1 but bundled npm 11.19.0; `npm doctor versions` requires npm 12.0.2.
- CI and deploy now run `npm install -g npm@latest` after setup-node, and use `actions/checkout@v7` plus `actions/setup-node@v7`.

## 2026-08-27 — Startup environment gate

- Added `npm run doctor` (`scripts/doctor.mjs`) as the session and fresh-clone environment gate.
- The doctor runs `npm doctor connection registry environment`, then checks Node.js 20+, git, `node_modules`, clasp credentials in `.secrets/`, `.clasp.json`, and anonymous Hello World visibility.
- `--fix` copies existing clasp credentials and runs `npm install`; `--ci` is toolchain-only for GitHub Actions.
- `package.json` now declares `engines.node >= 20`. `start.ai` runs the doctor at session start.
- Validation: `npm run build`, `npm test` (18 passing), and `npm run doctor -- --ci` passed. Full `npm run doctor` correctly fails on this checkout: develop ready, deploy not ready (missing `.secrets/.clasprc.json` and `.clasp.json`).


